:lumMod val="75000"/></a:schemeClr></a:solidFill><a:latin typeface="+mj-lt"/></a:rPr><a:t>Frontier Accelerate for Copilot: Envisioning &amp; POC </a:t></a:r><a:r><a:rPr lang="en-GB"/><a:t>to understand customer business priorities and focus on scenarios that are high-value for the organization.</a:t></a:r></a:p><a:p><a:r><a:rPr lang="en-US"/><a:t>We recommend the following customer roles to attend this engagement:</a:t></a:r></a:p></p:txBody></p:sp><p:sp><p:nvSpPr><p:cNvPr id="5" name="Content Placeholder 4"><a:extLst><a:ext uri="{FF2B5EF4-FFF2-40B4-BE49-F238E27FC236}"><a16:creationId xmlns:a16="http://schemas.microsoft.com/office/drawing/2014/main" id="{62B798E6-0DF8-1212-4CD6-8FE931ABF944}"/></a:ext></a:extLst></p:cNvPr><p:cNvSpPr><a:spLocks noGrp="1"/></p:cNvSpPr><p:nvPr><p:ph sz="quarter" idx="24"/></p:nvPr></p:nvSpPr><p:spPr><a:xfrm><a:off x="3418671" y="2019300"/><a:ext cx="2532888" cy="3927229"/></a:xfrm></p:spPr><p:txBody><a:bodyPr/><a:lstStyle/><a:p><a:pPr lvl="1"/><a:r><a:rPr lang="en-US" sz="1200"><a:solidFill><a:schemeClr val="accent1"><a:lumMod val="75000"/></a:schemeClr></a:solidFill><a:latin typeface="+mj-lt"/></a:rPr><a:t>Executive Project Sponsor, C-Suite or Sr. BDMs </a:t></a:r><a:r><a:rPr lang="en-US" sz="1200"/><a:t>(CFO, CMO, COO or relevant business leaders) who can sign off on proposed activities. </a:t></a:r></a:p><a:p><a:pPr lvl="1"/><a:r><a:rPr lang="en-US" sz="1200"><a:solidFill><a:schemeClr val="accent1"><a:lumMod val="75000"/></a:schemeClr></a:solidFill><a:latin typeface="+mj-lt"/></a:rPr><a:t>Business function/</a:t></a:r><a:br><a:rPr lang="en-US" sz="1200"><a:solidFill><a:schemeClr val="accent1"><a:lumMod val="75000"/></a:schemeClr></a:solidFill><a:latin typeface="+mj-lt"/></a:rPr></a:br><a:r><a:rPr lang="en-US" sz="1200"><a:solidFill><a:schemeClr val="accent1"><a:lumMod val="75000"/></a:schemeClr></a:solidFill><a:latin typeface="+mj-lt"/></a:rPr><a:t>department leads and knowledge workers </a:t></a:r><a:r><a:rPr lang="en-US" sz="1200"/><a:t>– who can participate in executive interviewing and interactive scenario prioritization, those who know best how their business works day-to-day and what end-user needs are.</a:t></a:r></a:p><a:p><a:pPr lvl="1"/><a:r><a:rPr lang="en-US" sz="1200"><a:solidFill><a:schemeClr val="accent1"><a:lumMod val="75000"/></a:schemeClr></a:solidFill><a:latin typeface="+mj-lt"/></a:rPr><a:t>Change Management, Training Leads and Corporate Communications </a:t></a:r><a:r><a:rPr lang="en-US" sz="1200"/><a:t>– integral to successful adoption, content providers, end user training and feedback planning is critical.</a:t></a:r></a:p><a:p><a:endParaRPr lang="en-US" sz="1400"/></a:p></p:txBody></p:sp><p:sp><p:nvSpPr><p:cNvPr id="6" name="Content Placeholder 5"><a:extLst><a:ext uri="{FF2B5EF4-FFF2-40B4-BE49-F238E27FC236}"><a16:creationId xmlns:a16="http://schemas.microsoft.com/office/drawing/2014/main" id="{43BD14D4-7E2D-F076-2869-AF00048B2DEC}"/></a:ext></a:extLst></p:cNvPr><p:cNvSpPr><a:spLocks noGrp="1"/></p:cNvSpPr><p:nvPr><p:ph sz="quarter" idx="25"/></p:nvPr></p:nvSpPr><p:spPr><a:xfrm><a:off x="6253141" y="2019300"/><a:ext cx="2532888" cy="2623795"/></a:xfrm></p:spPr><p:txBody><a:bodyPr/><a:lstStyle/><a:p><a:pPr lvl="1"/><a:r><a:rPr lang="en-US" sz="1200"><a:solidFill><a:schemeClr val="accent1"><a:lumMod val="75000"/></a:schemeClr></a:solidFill><a:latin typeface="+mj-lt"/></a:rPr><a:t>CIO, ITDM, IT Admin, Enterprise and Security Architects </a:t></a:r><a:r><a:rPr lang="en-US" sz="1200"/><a:t>– to provide architecture guidance and insights; technical guidance, visibility into currently deployed technologies and data security considerations.</a:t></a:r></a:p><a:p><a:pPr lvl="1"/><a:r><a:rPr lang="en-US" sz="1200"><a:solidFill><a:schemeClr val="accent1"><a:lumMod val="75000"/></a:schemeClr></a:solidFill><a:latin typeface="+mj-lt"/></a:rPr><a:t>Project Manager/Coordinator </a:t></a:r><a:r><a:rPr lang="en-US" sz="1200"/><a:t>– to provide overall engagement project management tasks, 